course: dictionary
lesson: 15924
title: Unprotected
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look inside the word. Un- means not, and protected means kept safe, so unprotected means not kept safe from harm. «The baby's hands were unprotected in the cold wind.» The hands had no gloves to keep them safe.
explain: The word can also mean not covered or shielded. «Her unprotected skin turned pink in the hot sun.» Skin with no cream or hat has nothing to shield it from the sun. Ask yourself: what would keep this safe, and is it there? If not, the word is unprotected.
explain: In computers, unprotected means there is no password or security. «The school file was unprotected, so anyone could open it.» The word can describe things, places and people, and it always means something that would keep them safe is missing.
fact: Unprotected means not kept safe from harm or danger.
fact: Unprotected means not covered or shielded, for example from sun or rain.
fact: In computing, an unprotected file has no password, so anyone can read it.
fact: «Unprotected iron rusts» because nothing covers it to keep out water and air.
fact: The opposite of unprotected is protected.
exercise: «The unprotected wires could give someone a nasty shock.» What does unprotected mean here? | * Not covered or kept safe | Brand new | Very loud | Very long
exercise: Iron left outside with no cover will rust. Which word describes that iron? | Famished | Ancient | Curt | * Unprotected
exercise: What is the opposite of unprotected? | Empty | Loud | Wet | * Protected
test: «The camp was unprotected, so the enemy could attack it easily.» What does unprotected mean in this sentence? | Newly built | * Not kept safe from attack | Full of happy children | Hidden under a thick blanket
test: Ella says a file with no password is unprotected. What does she mean? | It is covered in dust | * Anyone can open it because nothing keeps it safe | It has been locked with a password | It is very old and fragile
exam: «Without a hat or cream, his skin was unprotected in the sun.» What does unprotected mean? | Very hot to touch | Sunburnt and happy | Hidden in the shade | * Not covered or shielded from the sun
